        "procedure": "All operations were carried out under purified N2 or Ar. A mixture of NdCl3 (0.50 g, 2.0 mmol), H3L (0.59 g, 2.0 mmol), NaNH2 (0.40 g, 8.0 mmol) and Na2CO3 (0.20 g, 1.7 mmol) in thf (50 ml) was rapidly stirred at ambient temperature for 48 h, giving a light blue solution and a white precipitate. After filtration, concentration and addition of pentane (ca. 5 ml), dichroic light pink crystals of 1 deposited on prolonged standing (yield 66%).",
